From fc980e0ad4d4ef20de024668d6c313f8311289c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shkosugi <sin.kosugi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:15:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 35/37] System.Drawing.Common: built in the fork, for Windows
 and Linux; System.Web on it

WebFormsForCore.Drawing.Common builds the previous commit's source as System.Drawing.Common
10.0.1.0 (the Open key's token, cc7b13ffcd2ddd51: over Microsoft's 10.0.0.0, which is Windows
only since .NET 7), twice: FocTargetOS=windows (GDI+) and unix (libgdiplus, Mono's
implementation), by default the building machine's. The package has both (runtimes/win,
runtimes/unix; lib/ is the Windows build, as reference).

- System.Drawing.Common.Sources.props: the original project's source lists, as they are.
- Core\SR.generated.cs: the resource accessors dotnet/runtime's build generated, made from
  Resources\Strings.resx by experiments/wf4c/generate-drawing-sr.ps1 of the FrameworkOnCore
  repository.
- LibraryResolver: Unix without the System.Drawing.EnableUnixSupport switch .NET 6 required.
- For .NET 10, without warnings: Marshal.QueryInterface's IID passed as in, InvalidPrinterException's
  GetObjectData obsolete as its base (SYSLIB0051), CLS-compliant as dotnet/runtime builds it.
- Built without DEBUG in every configuration (a failed Debug.Assert ends a .NET process).
- WebFormsForCore.Web and WebFormsForCore.Drawing (net10.0) reference it instead of Microsoft's
  package.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
